      "content": "thanks for this. it's a really smooth summary. \n\ni was just glancing back at the raw numbers though, and i'm a little worried about the engineering numbers. i know you mentioned them as part of the \"natural fluctuations,\" but looking at the actual 25% figure, i'm concerned that if a Board member asks for the specific breakdown, the gap between what the summary implies and what the raw data shows will look like we're hiding something. \n\nis there a way we can adjust the wording for the engineering section? i want to steer clear of making it sound like a massive outlier that needs explaining. maybe we can characterize the engineering turnover more collectively with the other departments so it doesn't stand out as a crisis point?",
